        "headline_findings": [
          "2026 foliage forecast (high confidence): Seorak first color Oct 3, peak about Oct 16-25; low valleys (Sogongwon, Biseondae, Juongol) about Oct 20-30; Odaesan peak about Oct 16-25. The Oct 17-25 trip window sits on the peak, though a warm autumn may make color later than average.",
          "Seorak is crowded on weekends. Sokcho runs foliage traffic control Oct 3-Nov 8, 2026, with free lots B and C and shuttles. The file says to avoid Sat Oct 17, Sun Oct 18 and Sat Oct 24, and to do Seorak Mon Oct 19-Fri Oct 23, arriving before 07:00.",
          "The Seorak cable car to Gwongeumseong costs 16,000 KRW round trip (2026 fare). It is sold same-day on site only, with no advance booking. Weekend waits can top 1-2 hours. Buy tickets first, then hike Biseondae while waiting for the boarding time.",
          "Naksansa (founded 671, seaside, Uisangdae sunrise about 06:40, sea-cave Hongnyeonam) is the file's top Kamakura match. It is free since May 2023 and about 30 min by bus 9/9-1 from Sokcho. Hajodae, Hyuhyuam and the Jukdo/Ingu surf cafes make up the rest of that 'Kamakura/Shonan' day.",
          "Seorak, Naksansa and Woljeongsa are free to enter since the May 2023 abolition of heritage fees. Small fees: Ojukheon 3,000, Seongyojang 5,000, Badabuchae-gil about 5,000 (unverified).",
          "Onsen substitutes are partial. Cheoksan Hot Spring (about 10,000 KRW, nude single-sex outdoor bath in pines) is the most onsen-like. Seorak Waterpia (about 45,000, swimsuit) is a water park. Osaek Greenyard (hot-spring village at the foot of the Juongol trail) has unverified 2026 status. Seongyojang hanok (300-year-old estate) is the ryokan-like lodging but has no hot spring.",
          "Transport: KTX-Eum Seoul-Gangneung is about 2 h and 27,600 KRW (14 trains a day, 05:20 to 22:27). There is no rail to Sokcho or Yangyang. Gangneung-Sokcho by bus is 1-1h20 and about 7,500. Seoul-Sokcho bus is about 2h10-2h40 on weekdays, 3.5-4+ h on weekends, and about 25,000.",
          "Coast rail south (verified, timetables dated Oct 7 2026): KTX-Eum Gangneung to Gyeongju is about 2h45 and 34,300, leaving 09:36, 14:56 and 18:35. Gangneung to Busan Bujeon is 3h54-4h00 and 46,800. Gangneung to Pohang is about 2h21-2h28 and 28,700. Genuine sea views are mostly Gangneung-Jeongdongjin-Donghae-Samcheok. Sit on the left (east) side heading south.",
          "Odaesan fits on the way from Seoul to Gangneung. Get off at Jinbu station, then take a bus or a taxi (about 20,000) to Woljeongsa (fir-forest path, 1 km, National Treasure pagoda). The Seonjae-gil stream trail is 9 km, with peak color about Oct 18-28. Templestay costs about 70-90k pp.",
          "Juongol (Osaek) is the best red-maple gorge, peaking about Oct 18-28, and needs no reservation from Osaek. The Heullimgol start needs a KNPS advance reservation (5,000 a day cap) and has a rockfall-closure history.",
          "Food highlights: Jungang market dakgangjeong (Manseok), Abai village sundae and naengmyeon with the Gaetbae hand-pulled ferry (about 500-1,000), red snow crab in season (about 40,000 pp), Chodang tofu (11,000-16,000, go before 11:00), and Yangyang songi pine mushroom (about 40,000 pp, season ends mid to late October).",
          "Budget fit: the file estimates regional transport at under about 100,000 KRW pp, and the main paid sights are cheap. Lodging is the swing item: 3-person rooms run about 130k-800k KRW a night, and Saturdays in foliage season run 1.5-2x weekday rates."
        ],
