        "headline_findings": [
          "Verdict: Jeju is optional, not essential. Mainland (Seoul + Gyeongju + Busan, or Seoul + Seoraksan) matches their Japan favourites more directly (Gyeongju~Kamakura, Busan Blueline train~Enoden, Seoul~Shibuya).",
          "Jeju will not deliver peak foliage: Hallasan peak is forecast Nov 6, 2026, so Oct 20-24 shows only early or partial color. Seoraksan peaks about Oct 20 and gives more color.",
          "Jeju's real autumn assets are silver grass (peak mid-Oct to early Nov, prime for the trip dates), pink muhly, volcanic coast and haenyeo culture. Tangerines are still greenish until mid-Nov.",
          "Cost: 2 Jeju nights is about KRW 390,000-630,000 pp (about US$280-450), roughly 35-45% of the US$1,000 cap for about 25% of the nights. It includes 2 domestic flights, car or taxi, lodging and admissions.",
          "Timing: the 107th National Sports Festival (Oct 16-22) plus the Tamna Festival (Oct 17-21) tighten and raise flight, hotel and car prices. If going, do Jeju Oct 22-24 and book now.",
          "Best shape if chosen: Thu Oct 22 to Sat Oct 24, fly PUS-CJU (~1 h, KRW 50,000-90,000) in and CJU-GMP out Sat Oct 24 evening or early Sun Oct 25. This drops Gangwon and shortens Busan.",
          "Onsen analog: Pinx Podo Hotel (Itami Jun design, 42C aragonite hot-spring water in every room) at KRW 385,000-550,000 per night, about KRW 140,000-185,000 pp. Cheaper option: Sanbangsan carbonated hot spring, KRW 14,000 indoor.",
          "Driving needs a US licence plus a physical AAA IDP obtained before departure (no IDP, no rental). Realistic car cost is KRW 80,000-150,000/day with full insurance. Alternative: 8-h private taxi tour at KRW 164,000-200,000 per car (about KRW 55,000-67,000 pp for 3).",
          "Without a car, buses work only along the coastal corridors. Airport limousine 600 is KRW 5,500. Inland oreum, Yeongsil and forests need taxis.",
