          "Friday Oct 23 runs about 15-30% above weekdays. Saturday Oct 24 runs 1.4-1.8x weekdays, and Greenyard and the Sono-direct Sol Beach listing were already sold out. Kensington had no room for 3 on Tue Oct 20 and only 1-2 rooms on the other dates.",
          "Osaek Greenyard's spring and jjimjilbang are operating in Oct 2026 (live listing notices, plus an Aug 24, 2026 visit report). Open 06:00-22:00. Price: 18,000 public / 13,000 guest, or 28,000/20,000 with the jjimjilbang. Caveat: the signature carbonated pool is cool water, not a hot onsen.",
          "Cheoksan Hot Spring is confirmed for 2026: 53°C alkaline water, open daily 05:30-20:00 (outdoor baths until 19:00), 11,000 per adult, private family baths 50k/70k for 3 hours. It also rents rooms with in-room hot-spring tubs at 120k per night for 3-4 people (Oct 1-Nov 15 is its peak season). That is the best-value onsen-ryokan substitute, but booking is by Korean bank transfer or phone.",
          "Waterpia is NOT included with a room-only Sorano stay. Guests pay a discounted rate: 49,000 per adult for a low-season day pass (from Oct 12), 27,000 for the night spa. Sorano's '[10월] 추캉스 ALL INCLUSIVE' rate includes Waterpia and breakfast for 2 adults at 227k weekday / 256k Fri / 316k Sat, only 35k more than room-only.",
          "Seongyojang is confirmed live with many rooms for 3: Haengrangchae (sleeps 4, shared bathroom), Jungsarang (4 bedrooms, private bathroom), Choga (kitchen, private bathroom), Yeonjidang, and Seobyeoldang (nu-maru pavilion). Check-in 16:00, check-out 10:00; extra persons 15k each."
