        "file": "/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-rsalik-Library-Application-Support-Claude-scratch-workspaces-e6677c92-2974-4907-a0da-c7ac9ddbdf8c-66f568e9-f8bd-4c52-a222-d71c84fbd621-scratch-2026-10-07-778f00/6608af47-2359-4a74-81a2-d027e855f615/scratchpad/research/followup-gyeongbokgung_starlight_foreigner_booking.json",
        "headline_findings": [
          "Starlight foreigner sessions (Oct 21-24) are still sold out. The live Creatrip spot 13949 page shows isSoldOut=true as of Oct 6, 2026. Creatrip is the only channel in 2026; NOL World/Interpark Global is not used.",
          "Creatrip rules: max 2 tickets per person, so 3 travelers need 2 separate bookers. No same-day sales. Sales close at 23:59 KST two days before each date. Full refund only up to 3 days before, so released seats come back in ones and twos before that cutoff. Getting 3 seats in one session is a long shot.",
          "Session times settled: 18:20-20:10 and 19:30-21:20. Creatrip, Korea Times and Korean press all agree, so the 18:30/19:40 in events.json is wrong. Price is 60,000 KRW per person (US$44.81 on Creatrip). Max 38 per session and 8 sessions in total, so about 304 seats.",
          "Ticketlink general sessions do not run Oct 21-24 (those nights are foreigner-only). The only general nights in the trip are Oct 17-18: Korean-language, sold by lottery in August, and almost certainly gone.",
          "Fallback confirmed: Changgyeonggung 'Mulbit Yeonhwa' runs Oct 7 - Nov 1, Wed-Sun. The pond show is at 19:00, 19:30 and 20:00 and costs 1,000 KRW including admission (Ticketlink, max 4 per person; Creatrip for foreigners). It holds 400 per session. Only the pond scene needs a reservation; the rest of the light route is walk-up. The palace is open until 21:00 and closed Mondays.",
          "Weekly Wednesday Culture Day free entry applies: Deoksugung since Aug 2026; Changgyeonggung, Changdeokgung (not Huwon) and Jongmyo since Oct 2026. Gyeongbokgung is not included yet. So Wed Oct 21 is a free double-palace evening at Deoksugung (open to 21:00) plus Changgyeonggung/Mulbit."
        ],
        "top_recommendations": [
          {
            "name": "Do not pin the itinerary to Starlight",
            "why": "It is sold out, tickets are capped at 2 per buyer, and cancellations come back in small numbers. Keep Busan on Sat Oct 24 and the Gangwon weekdays as planned."
          },
          {
            "name": "Opportunistic Creatrip watch",
            "why": "If the Seoul nights land on Oct 21-23, two travelers should each check spot 13949 daily from about Oct 14 to each date's free-cancel cutoff (about Oct 18-20)."
          },
          {
            "name": "Book a Changgyeonggung Mulbit Yeonhwa slot for a Wed-Sun Seoul night",
            "why": "It costs 1,000 KRW, has 400 seats per session, and is a lit-palace evening by Chundangji pond in early foliage. It is also bookable for foreigners."
          },
          {
            "name": "Use Wed Oct 21 (or any Seoul Wednesday) for free palaces",
            "why": "Weekly Culture Day makes Deoksugung and Changgyeonggung free, and both stay open until 21:00."
          }
        ],
        "key_numbers": [
          "Starlight sessions: 18:20-20:10 and 19:30-21:20, about 110 min each",
          "Starlight price: 60,000 KRW per person (US$44.81; members US$42.12)",
          "Starlight capacity: 38 per session x 8 sessions = 304 seats; max 2 tickets per person",
          "Starlight sales close at 23:59 KST, 2 days before each date; full refund at 3 or more days before",
          "Mulbit Yeonhwa: Oct 7 - Nov 1, Wed-Sun, shows at 19:00/19:30/20:00, 1,000 KRW, 400 per session, max 4 per person",
          "Deoksugung and Changgyeonggung: 09:00-21:00 (last entry 20:00), closed Monday, 1,000 KRW, free on Wednesdays"
        ],
        "conflicts_or_uncertainties": [
          "Mulbit Yeonhwa remaining seats and the Creatrip listing for it were not checked live. An older bravo.etoday article says no reservation is needed (that is likely an earlier year's format).",
          "Wednesday free entry: the May 2026 Segye report and the yugacrew summary agree on the timeline, but I could not confirm an official royal.khs.go.kr October notice. It is unclear whether foreigners and evening hours are covered (no sign that they are excluded).",
          "The Starlight free-cancel cutoff is read from 'up to 3 days before'. The exact day Creatrip counts may differ by one day."
        ]
