        "domain": "followup-seorak_cablecar_heullimgol_bus_2026",
        "file": "/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-rsalik-Library-Application-Support-Claude-scratch-workspaces-e6677c92-2974-4907-a0da-c7ac9ddbdf8c-66f568e9-f8bd-4c52-a222-d71c84fbd621-scratch-2026-10-07-778f00/6608af47-2359-4a74-81a2-d027e855f615/scratchpad/research/followup-seorak_cablecar_heullimgol_bus_2026.json",
        "headline_findings": [
          "Seorak Cable Car hours, from the official live feed (/api/public/field-data, read Oct 7 2026): 08:30-17:30 on Oct 7-8 and 08:00-17:30 on Oct 9. Hours are set day by day, so expect about 08:00/08:30-17:30 on Oct 19-23.",
          "Cable car tickets: the adult round trip is 16,000 KRW (official 2026 fare table) and only round trips are sold. Tickets are sold on the day only, at the counter or kiosk, and each carries a boarding time. No per-person limit is published (the 1-per-person rule applies only to the Sokcho-resident discount).",
          "Heullimgol is OPEN for autumn 2026 and needs a reservation from Oct 1 to Nov 30. The cap is 5,000 a day in hourly slots of about 1,000. October entry is 08:00-15:00. One booking covers up to 10 people, and online booking closes at 14:00 the day before. Leftover places are registered on site at the Heullimgol Visitor Center.",
          "gangwon.json's 5,000/day cap is correct. The true reopening date is Sep 8 2022: it was planned for Sep 6 and delayed by Typhoon Hinnamnor, after a closure since a fatal rockfall in Aug 2015. foliage.json's '2024' is wrong. No 2026 rockfall closure was found; the trail closes on the day in rain or wind.",
          "Foreigners: the KNPS foreigner/English portal offers only shelters and campsites, not trail bookings. The Korean site needs Korean phone or i-PIN identity verification. The realistic options are weekday on-site leftover registration or a booking made by the hotel or a Korean contact.",
          "The Juongol out-and-back from Osaek to Yongso Falls needs no booking and allows two-way walking. Only the 3.1 km Heullimgol section (Visitor Center to Yongso junction) is booking-only and one-way.",
          "Fares after the Oct 1 2026 rise, Seoul Express Bus Terminal to Sokcho: standard 18,700, deluxe (udeung) 24,300, premium 31,500. Dong Seoul to Sokcho: deluxe 22,800, premium 29,600. Gangneung to Sokcho: mostly 8,400 (10,800 on slower runs)."
        ],
        "top_recommendations": [
          {
            "name": "Seorak weekday: cable car first, then Juongol",
            "why": "Be at the cable car counter by 08:00-08:30, walk Biseondae while waiting, then go to Osaek for Juongol in the afternoon. Juongol needs no booking."
          },
          {
            "name": "Heullimgol via on-site leftover registration or a hotel booking",
            "why": "Online booking needs Korean identity verification. At 5,000 a day, leftover places on a weekday morning are very likely."
          },
          {
            "name": "Book Seoul-Sokcho on the Kobus app or Klook with a foreign card",
            "why": "Deluxe from Gangnam costs 24,300 (about 2h35). October Friday and Sunday departures fill up."
          }
        ],
        "key_numbers": [
          "Cable car: 16,000 KRW adult round trip; 08:30-17:30 (Oct 7-8 2026), 08:00-17:30 on Oct 9; 50 people per cabin, every 5 min when busy; 19-min wait on a weekday midday on Oct 7",
          "Cable car refunds: full refund until 10 min before boarding, 20% fee after; no senior discount Sep 19-Nov 15 2026",
          "Heullimgol: 5,000/day, about 1,000/hour, Oct entry 08:00-15:00, booking closes 14:00 the day before, up to 10 per booking, fine 200,000-500,000 KRW",
          "Heullimgol section 3.1 km one-way; full route to Osaek 6.2 km, 3.5-4 h; reopened Sep 8 2022",
          "Seoul Express Terminal to Sokcho: 18,700 / 24,300 / 31,500 KRW; 45 a day, 06:00-23:30",
          "Dong Seoul to Sokcho: 22,800 / 29,600 KRW; 15 a day",
          "Gangneung to Sokcho: 8,400 KRW direct (about 1 h), 10,800 on slower runs; 22 a day"
        ],
        "conflicts_or_uncertainties": [
          "Bus fares came from asamaru timetable mirrors dated Oct 2-7 2026; kobus.co.kr refused connections, so the official site could not be checked directly.",
          "Foreign-card acceptance on Kobus (since Aug 2024) is based on news reports (Korea JoongAng Daily, KTO) and was not tested; whether the T-money intercity site takes foreign cards is unverified.",
          "The date Heullimgol bookings open is not published (an older guide says 14 days ahead). Whether a foreign phone or email can book is unverified, but likely not.",
          "There is no official data on weekday cable car sell-out times at the peak; the 1-3 h peak waits come from media reports.",
          "Some 2026 articles say Heullimgol was free with no booking Jan-Sep 2026 and needs a booking only Oct-Nov. A Sep 27 article says the Oct-Nov-only model starts in 2027. Either way, Oct 19-23 2026 needs a booking."
        ]
