          "The trains start at Gangneung. Stops: Jeongdongjin, Mukho, Donghae, Samcheok, Uljin, Yeongdeok, Pohang, Gyeongju, Taehwagang, Bujeon.",
          "The Donghae-line KTX-Eum started Dec 30, 2025 with 3 round trips a day. logistics.json's 2024 date is a year off. heritage's Dec 20 2024 is about the Jungang-line KTX-Eum stopping at Gyeongju, a different service, so it does not conflict.",
          "Booking window: since Oct 1 2026 tickets open 2 months before departure (announced by MOLIT/Korail). This does not change the advice: the whole trip already falls inside even the old 1-month window, so the group should book now.",
          "Fares after the Sep 1 2026 KTX-SRT merger (about 10% cut): Seoul-Gyeongju 44,500 and Gyeongju-Busan 10,100. heritage's 49,300 and ~11,000 are the old fares. Seoul-Busan is 54,400. Seoul-Gangneung 27,600 did not change.",
          "AREX Express: the official adult fare is 13,000. The 11,000 price is only for third-party vouchers (Klook, Trip.com, Waug).",
          "The Gangneung-Samcheok Sea Train is not running. Its last run was Dec 26, 2023, and Gangwon mentions a revival only as a future plan."
        ],
        "top_recommendations": [
          {
            "name": "Book KTX-Eum 752 (Gangneung 09:36 to Gyeongju 12:30) today",
            "why": "Only 3 KTX-Eum trains a day run this route, and tickets are already on sale. If 752 is sold out, take 754 (14:56 to 17:44) or the ITX-Maeum at 05:46."
          },
          {
            "name": "Use the post-merger fares in every costing",
            "why": "Seoul-Gyeongju 44,500, Gyeongju-Busan 10,100, Seoul-Busan 54,400, Seoul-Gangneung 27,600, Gangneung-Gyeongju 34,300, Gangneung-Bujeon 46,800, and AREX 13,000 (11,000 with a voucher)."
          },
          {
            "name": "Drop the Sea Train from all plans",
            "why": "It was retired in Dec 2023. The regular Donghae-line trains between Gangneung and Samcheok give the coastal views instead; sit on the left side heading south."
